<Pack>
	<!--
		THE CHAPTERS ARE NUMBERED IN THE FILENAME, and that is a deliberate departure from the
		convention the sibling libraries follow.

		In a library's help\, the patches are a flat set of HowTos that can be read in any order,
		so numbering the files makes every gap look like a broken install and Help.xml does the
		sequencing. Here the order is load bearing: chapter 05 assumes you know what a coordinate
		is, and reading them out of order does not work. VL.ExtendedTutorials numbers its Math
		series the same way, for the same reason - Explanation 01 Intro through 20 FPS Camera.

		Help.xml still carries the tags, and still groups the chapters into parts.
	-->
	<Topic title="Drawing data">
		<VLDocument link="05 Drawing GeoJSON on a map.vl" tags="geojson,map,mapsui,read,parse,feature,nts,netTopologySuite,style,styleByGeometry,label,marker,wgs84,mercator,projection,integration,packages" />
	</Topic>
